{title: How Can I Keep from Singing}
{artist: Robert Lowry}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: G}
{tempo: 60}
{time: 3/2}
{score: how-can-i-keep-from-singing.abc}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (How_Can_I_Keep_from_Singing-How_Can_I_Keep_from_Singing-Endless_Song-Singing-My_Life_Flows_On) and the Cyber Hymnal score (100% of syllables agree)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]My [G]life flows on in [C]endless song;
[C]A[G]bove earth's lamen[D]tation.
[D]I [Bm]catch the [G]sweet, though [C]faroff hymn
[C]That [G]hails a new creation;
[G]Through all the tumult [D]and the [G]strife,
[G]I hear that music ringing;
[G]It finds an echo [C]in my [G]soul...
[G]How [Bm]can I [G]keep from singing?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]What [G]though my joys and [C]comforts die?
[C]The [G]Lord my Savior [D]liveth;
[D]What [Bm]though the [G]darkness [C]gather round!
[C]Songs [G]in the night He giveth:
[G]No storm can shake my [D]inmost [G]calm
[G]While to that refuge clinging;
[G]Since Christ is Lord of [C]Heav’n and [G]earth,
[G]How [Bm]can I [G]keep from singing?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]I [G]lift mine eyes; the [C]cloud grows thin;
[C]I [G]see the blue a[D]bove it;
[D]And [Bm]day by [G]day this [C]pathway smoothes
[C]Since [G]first I learned to love it:
[G]The peace of Christ makes [D]fresh my [G]heart,
[G]A fountain ever springing:
[G]All things are mine since [C]I am [G]His—
[G]How [Bm]can I [G]keep from singing?
{end_of_verse}
